lls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Kansas remains a Republican-leaning state in presidential politics, and with no incumbent on the ballot neither side gains an incumbency edge. No public polls or expert ratings target this contest directly, so the race's standing rests on the state's partisan fundamentals. Recent statewide polling sentiment shows voters wanting a check on the administration and trusting Democrats more on issues, and Democratic candidates ran unusually well across red states in the 2026 midterms.\n\nThose signals justify a modest shift toward Democrats from pure fundamentals, but Kansas has favored Republicans by wide margins in recent presidential cycles, and the Republican field appears to be consolidating early behind a strong frontrunner. The result is a Republican edge of roughly six points with wide uncertainty. A sustained Democratic wave or unusual turnout could narrow the gap; a return to normal presidential-year dynamics would widen it.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1844, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2276, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2132, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2313, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.227, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2296, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2252, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2505, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2283, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2402, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2622, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2232, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2736, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2699, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2412, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2596, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2591, "margin": -6.5}, {"